cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this idea or software, please cite it as below."
title: "Common Ground: a knowledge graph as a shared medium for communication between humans and language models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gray"
    given-names: "Nicholas"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ndg13b/CommonGround"
abstract: >-
  A prototype in which humans and language models build a knowledge graph
  together. Every link carries a rationale, participants record agreement,
  disagreement or uncertainty with reasons, revisions supersede rather than
  overwrite, and multi-hop answers report their weakest link. The graph
  serves as common ground: a shared, inspectable record of how human and
  model understanding converge.
keywords:
  - knowledge graph
  - large language models
  - human-AI collaboration
  - common ground
  - retrieval-augmented generation
